I've found a workaround for this bug. The issue is that OpenCode's custom tools don't handle object returns properly - it tries to call `.split()` on non-string values.
**Workaround**: Change your custom tool to return ONLY a string instead of an object.
Example fix in yaml_edit.ts:
// BEFORE (causes text2.split error):
return {
  results,
  summary: `${successCount} succeeded, ${errorCount} errors`
}
// AFTER (works):
const outputLines = results.map(r => 
  `${r.file}: ${r.status} - ${r.message}`
)
return outputLines.join('\n') + '\nSummary: ${successCount} succeeded...`
This fixed the text2.split is not a function error in my custom yaml_edit tool.
